Sure! Below is a simple example of an HTML card that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only CSS (no JavaScript) and works in modern browsers.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container to center the card */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* Card wrapper */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D transform */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
    width:300px;
    height:200px;
    background:#fff;
    border-radius:12px;
    box-shadow:0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    transition:transform .6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;    /* Needed for 3D children */
    cursor:pointer;
    position:relative;
}

/* Front & back faces */
.card-face {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;     /* Hide backside when rotated */
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    font-size:1.5rem;
    color:#333;
    border-radius:12px;
}

.card-front {
    background:#4CAF50;
    color:white;
}

.card-back {
    background:#2196F3;
    color:white;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* Start hidden behind front */
}

/* Hover effect */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);       /* Flip the card */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            Front Side
        </div>
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            Back Side
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` has `perspective: 1000px;` which gives the 3D effect.
2. **Transform style** – The `.card` uses `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its child elements keep their 3D positioning.
3. **Backface visibility** – Each face (`.card-face`) hides its backside with `backface-visibility:hidden;`.
4. **Hover rotation** – On hover, the card rotates 180 degrees around the Y‑axis, revealing the back side.

Feel free to replace the text or add images inside the `.card-front` and `.card-back` divs. You can also tweak colors, sizes, or transition timing to fit your design.
